--- a/saas/README.md
+++ b/saas/README.md
@@ -24,6 +24,48 @@ After making changes to this gem, you need to update Fizzy to pick up the change
 BUNDLE_GEMFILE=Gemfile.saas bundle update --conservative fizzy-saas
 ```
 
+## Billing configuration
+
+Hosted billing uses Stripe Checkout and the customer portal. Configure these environment variables:
+
+* `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`: the secret API key for this environment.
+* `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`: the signing secret for `/stripe/webhooks`.
+* `STRIPE_MONTHLY_V1_PRICE_ID`: the USD recurring **$20/month Unlimited** price (5 GB).
+* `STRIPE_MONTHLY_EXTRA_STORAGE_V1_PRICE_ID`: the USD recurring **$25/month Unlimited+** price (500 GB).
+
+These price-variable names are retained for compatibility with the deployment secrets.
+Create/configure the two prices in Stripe and enable subscription changes and cancellation
+in the customer portal. Subscribe the webhook endpoint to `customer.subscription.created`,
+`customer.subscription.updated`, and `customer.subscription.deleted`. Run the SaaS database
+migrations (`SAAS=1 bin/rails db:migrate`) before deploying.
+
+Free accounts have 1,000 published cards and 1 GB of storage. Drafts do not count.
+Only account admins/owners can open billing or create checkout/portal sessions.
+Checkout redirects do not grant access; signed subscription webhooks do. Active and
+trialing subscriptions receive their paid allowance; other statuses fall back to Free.
+Scheduled cancellation retains access until Stripe reports the subscription ended.
+
+Staff can manage accounts at `/admin/accounts`. Comp provides Unlimited+ allowances
+without modifying the Stripe subscription; Uncomp restores the underlying plan.
+Usage overrides replace the measured card count and/or bytes used, not the quota.
+Blank fields use measured usage, zero is valid, and Reset deletes the override.
+Existing per-account storage exceptions continue to take precedence over plan storage.
+
+### Offline billing tests
+
+No Stripe account, credentials, or network connection is required for these tests:
+
+```sh
+SAAS=1 DATABASE_ADAPTER=sqlite RAILS_ENV=test PARALLEL_WORKERS=1 bin/rails test \
+  saas/test/models/account/billing_test.rb \
+  saas/test/controllers/account/billings_controller_test.rb \
+  saas/test/controllers/card/card_limited_test.rb \
+  saas/test/controllers/admin/accounts_controller_test.rb \
+  saas/test/controllers/stripe/webhooks_controller_test.rb
+```
+
+Stripe sessions are mocked; webhook requests use real locally generated signatures.
+
